From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:00:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 124/128] Status bar: show line, selection, counts and file
 info at the bottom

A thin bar under the find and go-to bars, off by default (View > Status
bar, or the switch in Settings > Appearance), for the active editor tab
(the focused view's when split). Left: the cursor line and column, the
selection size or the column block, as a button that opens Go to line.
Right: lines, characters and (Markdown only) words, the line endings,
the encoding and the indentation.

Every editor tab keeps a generation number that goes up when its text
changes: in TabChanged (paste, cut, undo, redo, replace, mirrored
clones, line ending conversion), when a key or input method text in the
text box changed the lines around the cursor, selection or column
block, and on load and reload. The counts are cached per generation, so
an unchanged text is never counted again. A selection over 100,000
lines shows its line count only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

